From 82811b9b2e40e3ce26eb4146d4b77824cafa2fea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 04:22:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Wire real logos into the "Trusted by" strip; AMD swap +
 Custom Analog Layout rename

Replaces the text-only "Trusted by" list with each partner's actual
logo image (assets/images/trust-logos/), sized consistently via CSS
(height 44px desktop / 34px mobile, object-fit: contain) instead of
font styling.

Fixed two issues in the supplied files before wiring them in:
- akrostar.svg was actually a JPEG (confirmed via file signature),
  not an SVG -- renamed to akrostar.jpg so the browser decodes it
  correctly instead of trying to parse binary JPEG data as XML.
- That JPEG had ~75% empty white padding around the actual logo mark
  (a 5626x1920 canvas with a small centered logo), which made it
  render as a barely-visible sliver at strip height. Cropped it down
  to the actual logo content (3596x370) using ffmpeg's cropdetect on
  an inverted copy (to detect the white background as croppable).

Also bundles two pending changes that hadn't landed yet:
- Swap HiSilicon for AMD in the trust strip
- Rename "Custom Analog Design" to "Custom Analog Layout" sitewide

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SjcntVjf5Nr2bdomgFdfPu
